branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.44. Fixes a false early heart-rate lock. Your log showed the reading
  "lock" at 105 bpm a second after you put your finger down, then drift 100→53→72 — but that
  105 wasn't a pulse, it was the finger still settling/pressing (the filtered signal swung
  ~0.76, where a real pulse swings ~0.03–0.08, and the periodicity was weak). A steady wobble
  can fool a beat-counter into a confident-looking-but-wrong rate. Fix: the analyzer now
  recognises that an over-large swing is MOTION, not pulse, skips those frames, and lets the
  confidence fall so a wobble can neither grab nor hold a lock — the BPM only commits once a
  real, calm pulse is present. Pure, unit-tested, camera-analysis path only (not audio/render/
  launch). dsp-reviewer: GO.
  Test: 10.76.45 → Start, put finger on lens but move/press a bit first: it should stay
  "Reading…/Cover camera" instead of jumping to a wrong high number; once you hold still it
  locks onto your real rate and holds steady. Menus stay selectable; number pad −/+ unchanged.
